update content_bodies set title = '太鼓まつりに参加してみた2024', description = '今年7月に行われたやわたの夏の風物詩、太鼓まつり。屋形太鼓(みこし)の上でうちわを振って鼓舞する「あぶ手」視点の映像や、石清水八幡宮の参道で行われた宮入の様子などを動画にまとめました。' where id = '0qnaU0gwlFE2Nxp5kpTSq';
update content_bodies set title = 'Participating in the Taiko Festival 2024', description = 'In July this year, the Yawata Summer Festival, known for its taiko drums, took place. This video compilation features footage from the perspective of the ''Abute'' performers, who encourage the crowd by waving fans atop the yatai (float). It also includes scenes from the shrine entrance ceremony held along the approach to the Iwashimizu Hachimangu Shrine.' where id = 'FkexG5b5CQFfMn3-U_54A';
update content_bodies set title = '【京都府八幡市】男山散策動画　|　石清水八幡宮と豊かな自然', description = 'この動画では、石清水八幡宮の境内にある男山の散策路や史跡、石垣を紹介しています。男山は、ブラタモリでも取り上げられた場所で、竹林が広がり、自然を感じられる散策路があります。また、かつて48近くの寺が存在した「男山四十八坊」の跡地も多く残っており、石垣が歴史を物語っています。自然と歴史に触れながら、男山を散策してみませんか？' where id = 'kXmyZgSBWmlblnINsVnMA';
update content_bodies set title = 'Exploring Otokoyama in Yawata City, Kyoto | Iwashimizu Hachimangu Shrine and Rich Nature', description = 'This video showcases the Otokoyama walking trail and historical sites within the Iwashimizu Hachimangu Shrine grounds. Otokoyama, featured in the program ''Buratamori,'' is home to a bamboo grove and a scenic walking path that allows visitors to experience nature. The area was once known for the ''Otokoyama Shijuhachibo,'' which included nearly 48 temples, many of which have remnants of stone walls, providing a glimpse into the past. Come and explore the natural beauty and history of Otokoyama!' where id = 'X_Oiik4B_5Yuz8fxocXER';
